  <p>The message was Hebrew before it was Greek. Yahushua and His apostles spoke and taught in Hebrew, and the earliest witnesses say their message was first written in Hebrew. The Greek came later — “translated into Greek, though by what author is uncertain” (Jerome). Plato never sat at the feet of Gamaliel, yet somehow his ideas made it into the translation. The words below are the translators’, not the apostles’.</p>
